== 20th-21st century Baliscan architecture ==

=== Contemporary indigenous architecture ===

Indigenous architectural traditions continue to influence contemporary Baliscan construction, particularly in rural and culturally conservative communities. Wallche pueblos maintain active building programs employing traditional adobe techniques alongside modern construction; the [[Pueblo Revival]] style of the late 20th century drew explicitly upon Wallche vernacular forms. Contemporary Kurupiranga communities in the Marañón interior continue to construct oka for ceremonial purposes, even where everyday dwellings employ modern materials. The ''Quilombo Vernacular'' style, emphasizing communal space, natural materials, and defensive privacy, has influenced community housing projects throughout the confederation.

The integration of indigenous architectural knowledge into contemporary practice has been facilitated by the [[Confederal Indigenous Architecture Program]], established in 1978 to document, preserve, and transmit traditional building techniques. The program has sponsored reconstruction of historical structures, apprenticeship programs pairing elder craftspeople with young builders, and architectural competitions incorporating indigenous forms and principles. The resulting synthesis—termed ''Neo-Indigenist'' architecture by critics—represents one of the most distinctive contributions of Baliscan architecture to global design discourse.
